$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1,1,4-Triphenyl-1-buten-3-yne5 (7). To a
suspension of PdCl2(dppf) (9 mg, 0.025 mmol, 5 mol %) in THF (2.5 mL) in
a Schlenk tube was added 2a (82.5 mg, 0.25 mmol) followed by iodobenzene
(51 mg, 0.25 mmol) at room temperature under N2. After aqueous 3 M KOH
(0.75 mmol, 0.25 ml) was added, the reaction mixture turned deep brown
immediately. The reaction mixture was stirred for overnight at room
temperature. After the reaction was complete, the reaction mixture was
quenched with sat. NH4Cl solution and then extracted with ethyl acetate
(10 mL x 2). The combined organic layers were washed with brine and dried
over MgSO4. Isolation by silica gel chromatography.
(E)-1-Methyl-1,4-diphenyl-1-buten-3-yne6 (8). Following the preparation
procedure of compound 7, the title compound was isolated in 76% yield
(41.5 mg). 1H NMR: δ 7.53-7.46 (m, 4H), 7.40-7.29 (m, 6H), 6.12 (q, J =
1.1 Hz, 1H), 2.41 (d, J = 1.1 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 148.4,
141.0, 131.5, 128.6, 128.5, 128.2, 128.1, 125.6, 123.9, 106.7, 95.4,
88.4, 18.8.
